course: dictionary
lesson: 14003
title: Words that paint a picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words do more than name a thing. They paint a picture in the reader's mind. «The lumbering giant stomped across the valley.» The words giant and stomped are heavy and big, so lumbering must mean moving slowly and heavily.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The slow, heavy giant stomped across the valley» still makes sense, so you are right. Always ask: what does the word tell me about the thing it describes?
explain: Lumbering can also be a verb, an action word. «The bear was lumbering along the riverbank.» Here it shows the bear walking in a heavy, clumsy way. Lumber, lumbers, lumbered and lumbering all belong to one word family.
fact: Lumbering means moving slowly, heavily and clumsily.
fact: Lumbering can describe giants, trolls, dinosaurs, bears or old buses.
fact: As a verb, «lumbering» shows a heavy, clumsy way of walking: «lumbering along».
fact: In North America, lumbering means cutting down trees and preparing the wood to sell.
fact: Lumbering was a big industry in the history of Canada and the USA.
exercise: «The lumbering troll crossed the bridge.» What does lumbering mean here? | Flying high in the sky | *Moving slowly and heavily | Running very fast and light | Singing loudly
exercise: «The old bus was lumbering up the hill.» What is the bus doing? | Flying over the hill | *Moving slowly and heavily | Making a loud siren noise | Stopping suddenly
exercise: In the history of Canada, lumbering was a big industry. What is lumbering in this sense? | Walking slowly in the woods | *Cutting down trees and preparing wood to sell | Painting pictures of forests | Building bridges over rivers
test: «The lumbering dinosaur shook the ground with every step.» What does lumbering suggest about the dinosaur? | Hungry for fish | *Big, heavy and slow | Invisible and silent | Tiny and quick
test: Which sentence uses lumbering as a verb, an action? | «The lumbering giant was tall.» | «We saw a lumbering bear.» | *«The bear was lumbering along the path.» | «The lumbering troll was happy.»
exam: «The lumbering robot crossed the playground, its metal feet clanking.» What does lumbering tell the reader about the robot? | Tiny and silent | Soft and furry | *Big, heavy and slow | Quick and light
